# Rename this file to `private_key.local`, then paste your BULK master
# account's base58 private key on the line below -- one line, no quotes,
# nothing else.
#
# `private_key.local` is git-ignored and never leaves your machine. Once the
# key is in, encrypt it from the menu: Accounts Management -> Encrypt Private
# Key. The file is then replaced by an encrypted envelope and the bot asks for
# your password at startup.
#
# A sub-account has no key of its own. It is created by, and signed for by,
# the master -- so this one key is all the bot needs, and the bot finds your
# sub-account by itself.

